======================================================================
PART D — DATA PROVENANCE AND EVALUATION DEPENDENCIES
======================================================================

1. Training data (the basis of the Part B restriction)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

The synthetic training set produced by data/generate_synthetic_dataset.py is
rendered from two third-party asset collections:

  * Replica Dataset — https://github.com/facebookresearch/Replica-Dataset
    Replica Research Terms: non-commercial research or educational use only,
    and that restriction carries over to derivative works, including trained
    models.

  * Google Scanned Objects — https://app.gazebosim.org/GoogleResearch
    CC BY 4.0. Attribution: Downs et al., "Google Scanned Objects: A
    High-Quality Dataset of 3D Scanned Household Items", ICRA 2022.

checkpoints/best_model.pth was trained on renders of these assets. Its
noncommercial restriction is independent of the license we grant in Part B and
cannot be waived by us.

2. Pretrained backbone
----------------------------------------------------------------------

The encoder is initialised from torchvision's ImageNet-pretrained ResNet-34
(torchvision, BSD-3-Clause). ImageNet imagery itself is distributed for
non-commercial research use.

3. Evaluation dependencies (not redistributed here)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

The evaluation scripts drive third-party trackers, matchers and refiners that
you clone and download separately, each under its own license. See the tables
in README.md for the upstream repositories. Notable terms:

  * SuperGlue (magicleap/SuperGluePretrainedNetwork) — weights are released
    under a license restricting use to non-commercial research; obtain them
    from upstream under those terms.
  * CoTracker3, TAPIR, LocoTrack, LightGlue, DISK, ALIKED, LoFTR,
    ASpanFormer, S2DNet, Patch2Pix, COTR, CAPS, glue-factory — see each
    upstream repository.

4. Benchmark datasets
----------------------------------------------------------------------

TAP-Vid (DAVIS / Kinetics / RGB-Stacking), HPatches, MegaDepth and ScanNet are
obtained from their maintainers under their own terms. ScanNet in particular
requires signing a terms-of-use agreement.
